/* game-settings.js - the player's in-game settings, once per game (D431).

   Owner, 2026-10-22: "before a user can use AI Scripts it forces them to say
   their in-game settings like sensitivity, ADS sensitivity and deadzones for
   every game ... these settings can be changed or customized in Device
   always, but AI Scripts isn't usable until they set their in-game settings".

   Why: a ready-made gun script (anti-recoil above all) is a stick push made
   on its maker's settings. With both sets known, the push is scaled so the
   turn it makes in the game is the same on the player's settings
   (sensitivity, ADS, the deadzone the game cuts off). D432: a shared Script
   carries its maker's set (`madeWith`) and is scaled to the player's on
   paste, on a linear model until each game's measured curve replaces it.

   One copy per GAME: saved into every config of that game (as the gun
   reader's box is, name-reader.js boxSaved), and a config of a game that
   another config already answered for counts as answered.

   window.ZSGAMESET:
     of(p)            the settings for p's game, or null
     needs(p)         true while AI Scripts must ask first
     gateHTML(p)      AI Scripts' screen until they are given
     deviceCardHTML(p) the card on Device (always there, always editable)
     wire(root, p, done) wires either form; done() after a save
     save(p, vals)    writes them to every config of p's game
     scaleStick(x, y, from, to, {ads})  D432: a push on `from` -> on `to`
